<title>JAPAN: Tokyo-Mitsubishi reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Tokyo-Mitsubishi reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	   139.65	   424.51</p>
<p>  Bad loans			490.75	   228.01</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	 561.86	   503.64</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients  252.56	   251.17</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    1.44 trln	1.41 trln</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
